{{!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  home/training-illustration.hbs — the homepage's training artwork.

  It draws the REAL thing: the same rail the curriculum sidebar renders — square
  section nodes, round module dots, and a blue fill that stops at "you are
  here". Showing the actual product beats generic art, and it means the
  homepage promise matches the page it links to.

  Design-system rules this follows (see CLAUDE.md / assets/css/theme):
    • flat — solid fills, hairline strokes, no gradients / glass / glow
    • ONE working blue; everything else is surface + ink
    • role tokens only (fill-surface-raised, stroke-border, …) so it flips in
      dark mode for free — the old training-trail.svg was fixed light-canvas
      art, which is why the section around it had to hard-code navy inks.
    • the single sanctioned motion is the gentle float, and only motion-safe.

  Purely decorative: aria-hidden, with the meaning carried by the copy beside it.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<svg viewBox="0 0 460 380" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
     class="h-auto w-full max-w-[30rem] motion-safe:animate-float" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">

